<description>
Mark every complete square object with red pixels just outside its corners.

Input structure:
- A uniform background contains one or more monochrome 4-connected foreground objects.
- The relevant objects are square frames or filled squares: their bbox is square
  and all cells on the bbox border have the object's color.
- Non-square bars and incomplete fragments may also appear and are ignored.

Rule:
- Keep the input unchanged.
- For each complete square object, paint red on the two outside background
  pixels orthogonally adjacent to each of the square's four corners.

Key insight: The transformation is not based on size or color; it selects
objects whose bounding box is a complete square border and labels only their
exposed outer corner-adjacent cells.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "monochrome 4-connected foreground objects on the background; some objects have a complete square bbox border",
  "transform": "for each object whose bbox is square and whose bbox border is fully foreground, paint red on the two outside background pixels orthogonally adjacent to each of its four corners; leave bars and incomplete fragments unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10, background=7 (orange) [observed]
  foreground_color: single non-bg, non-red color per grid; observed {6, 8}
  squares:
    count: 1-4 complete-square-border objects
    size: 2-8; size 2 => filled 2x2 block; size 3-8 => hollow frame (border filled, interior bg)
    placement: each square needs margin >= 1 from grid edge (for corner markers)
    nesting: a small square may sit inside a larger frame's interior (train_2 shows 2x2 inside 8x8)
    corner_markers: 8 bg cells per square (2 per corner, orthogonally adjacent outside) must all be bg and in-bounds
    no marker overlap: marker positions of different squares must not collide
  distractors:
    count: 0-5 non-square foreground objects, same color as squares
    types: single pixels, horizontal/vertical bars, filled rectangles with non-square bbox
    must not form a complete square border (non-square bbox, or 1x1)
  transform:
    keep input unchanged; for each complete square, paint RED (2) at the 8 corner-adjacent outside cells
    corner formula: for bbox (r0,c0,r1,c1) -> (r0-1,c0),(r0,c0-1),(r0-1,c1),(r0,c1+1),(r1+1,c0),(r1,c0-1),(r1+1,c1),(r1,c1+1)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction with placement validation
  steps:
    1. Choose grid 10x10, bg=7, pick one foreground color from {6, 8} (or any non-bg, non-red)
    2. Choose 1-4 square sizes (2-8). For each, decide frame (size>=3) or filled (size=2).
    3. Place squares one at a time on the grid with margin >= 1 from edges. After placing,
       verify all 8 marker positions are in-bounds, currently bg, and not occupied by prior
       squares or their markers. Allow nesting (small inside large frame interior).
    4. Place 0-5 distractors (pixels, bars, rectangles) in remaining bg space.
       Ensure no distractor accidentally completes a square border.
    5. Build output by copying input and painting RED at each square's 8 corner-marker positions.
```
